  message: "Setting to needs_human_review pending architectural decision: the fix requires either (a) a new pre-pass that builds a function-return-type registry from method/function declarations across all Go source files, then resolves call expression types via this registry, or (b) accepting that name-based heuristic resolution will continue to misroute common methods like Close/Add/Context/Set when the receiver type isn't directly inferable. Option (a) is a substantial addition; option (b) leaves global name collisions in place. Recommend human triage before committing to a direction. Not a regression — this gap has been present and was only surfaced because INV-kunam fix made the prometheus slice now reach into web/api/v1/api.go where the misresolutions are visible."  # 7483
